WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.370
Look at the label inside a T-shirt.

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.150
It might say: made in Bangladesh.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.310
There, ready-made garments
were about 85 per cent of all

4
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:12.820
exports in 2022 to 2023.

5
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.010
The UK is the other way round.

6
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.880
More than half of what it
sells abroad is services,

7
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.390
not goods. So why do countries
buy so much from abroad,

8
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:25.750
and does open trade leave
everyone better off?

9
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.230
In this mission, you'll put two
countries' workers to the test,

10
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:33.000
and see what happens to output
when each one specialises.

11
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.330
Then you'll look at what the UK trades,

12
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.640
and weigh up the case for
and against free trade.

13
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.620
Your mission: find out
why countries trade,

14
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.430
and whether open trade
really leaves everyone ahead.
